---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const updated = '2026-09-07';
---

<Base
  title="Terms & Conditions | The Cone Sleeves"
  description="The terms that govern use of theconesleeves.com and the custom printing work we quote, proof and produce for you."
  path="/terms-conditions/"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Terms &amp; Conditions', path: '/terms-conditions/' }]}
>
  <section class="section-tight" style="background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--paper-blush),var(--paper))">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-line">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="form-note">Last updated 7 September 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-narrow prose">
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of theconesleeves.com and the custom printing work we quote and
        produce. Please read them before placing an order. If you do not agree with them, do not
        use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>What we sell</h2>
      <p>
        We manufacture custom printed packaging to order: cone sleeves, food sleeves and trays,
        made to your specification and your artwork. This is a business-to-business printing
        service. The website does not take payment and there is no checkout &mdash; every order
        begins with a written quote and is confirmed by email.
      </p>

      <h2>Quotes</h2>
      <p>
        A quote is based on the size, quantity, board, printing and finish you describe. If any of
        those change, the price changes with them and we will re-quote before proceeding. Unless
        the quote itself says otherwise, it is valid for 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>Artwork and proofs</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for holding the rights to any logo, image, typeface or text you send
        us, and for confirming that your artwork is correct. We supply a digital proof before
        printing and nothing goes to press until you approve it in writing. Once a proof is
        approved, errors it contained &mdash; including spelling, color build and layout &mdash;
        are not grounds for a reprint at our cost.
      </p>

      <h2>Color and dimensions</h2>
      <p>
        Screens and presses do not render color identically, and no monitor is a reliable proof of
        a printed color. Slight variation between a screen preview and the printed result, and
        between print runs, is normal in commercial printing. Cutting and folding carry a small
        tolerance, which we allow for in every dieline.
      </p>

      <h2>Production and delivery</h2>
      <p>
        Standard production is 6&ndash;7 business days from proof approval, and a rush option of
        3&ndash;4 business days is available on request. Those windows cover manufacturing only.
        Delivery time depends on the carrier and destination, and while we give estimates in good
        faith we cannot guarantee a carrier&rsquo;s performance or events outside our control.
      </p>

      <h2>Custom work, cancellation and returns</h2>
      <p>
        Because every item is printed to your specification, orders cannot be cancelled once they
        have gone to press, and custom-printed goods are not returnable for a change of mind.
        Inspect your delivery on arrival. If goods arrive damaged, or the printing does not match
        the proof you approved, contact us within 14 days of delivery at
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will reprint or refund the affected
        portion of the order.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The text, images, layout and code on this site belong to {SITE.name} or our suppliers and
        are protected by copyright and trademark law. You may not copy or reuse them without our
        written consent. Your own artwork remains yours; sending it to us grants only the license
        we need to quote, proof, print and reprint your job.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Do not use this site for any unlawful purpose, and do not attempt to disrupt it or to
        interfere with anyone else&rsquo;s use of it. We may refuse work that infringes a third
        party&rsquo;s rights or that we consider unlawful.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent the law allows, our liability for any order is limited to the amount paid for
        that order. We are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, including lost profit
        or lost business, arising from a delay or a defect.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        We may revise these terms; the date at the top shows when they last changed, and the terms
        in force when you place an order are the ones that apply to it. Questions go to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or {SITE.phone}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
